claim.claim-text:
(a) providing a first roll of facer material, the first roll of facer material being woven and having a tensile strength greater than 356 N/76 mm (80 lbf/3 inch) in both a machine direction and a cross direction and a weight of 20 to 200 grams per square meter;
(b) providing a second roll of facer material, the second roll of facer material being woven and having a tensile strength greater than 356 N/76 mm (80 lbf/3 inch) in both a machine direction and a cross direction and a weight of 20 to 200 grams per square meter; and
(c) sandwiching a foam between the first and second rolls of facer material to form an insulation board assembly that when adhered or mechanically fastened onto a roof assembly permits the roof assembly to meet the Very Severe Hail rating of FM 4470 (Class 1).
